{
  "agent": "holmes-native",
  "artifact_text": "**Observations**\n- Pod logs for `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` show repeating `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)` errors.\n- Deployment `billing-api` in `demo-apps` sets `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` to `900` seconds.\n- Custom resource `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` in `ack-system` configured `idleClientTimeout` to `600` seconds (change `CI-2452`).\n\n**Ruled-out leads**\n- Memory exhaustion was ruled out because heap warnings and rising RSS are symptoms of pool exhaustion holding request objects (incident `INC-2024-0312`).\n- Load balancer timeouts were ruled out because the ALB idle timeout was raised to 120s and HTTP keep-alive to 125s (change `CI-2455`).\n\n**Root cause**\nThe database connection pool exhausts because RDS Proxy's `idleClientTimeout` (600s) is shorter than `billing-api`'s pool recycling delay (900s), dropping idle sockets prematurely.\n\n**Recommended action**\nThe infrastructure team should remove or raise `idleClientTimeout` on `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` above 900 seconds following runbook `RB-014`.",
